The requested enrichment fetch is not included. It needs `aap:caps/http-client`, and this node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`. Importing anything else would exceed its authority. The output is unchanged either way.

The node marks every considered id as seen, but only when the digest was actually published. An unpublished digest records nothing, so those items are retried on the next run.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        if published.published {
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                recorded += 1;
            }
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
